course: dictionary
lesson: 6099
title: Big city words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a clue to another word. «In 1829 Robert Peel set up London's Metropolitan Police.» London is a very big city, and the word Metropolitan sits next to it, so metropolitan probably links to big cities.
explain: Metropolitan means belonging to a very big city, called a metropolis, and the towns around it. Try it in the sentence: «London's big-city police» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Metropolitan can also be a job title in church. «Metropolitan Andrey Sheptytsky's network hid Jewish children.» Here Metropolitan is a title, a senior bishop, not a place. The word before a name often tells you what kind of word it is.
fact: Metropolitan is an adjective, so it describes things like a city, an area or a police force.
fact: A metropolis is a very big city, and the towns around it are its suburbs.
fact: A metropolitan area is a big city plus its suburbs, such as the Sydney metropolitan area.
fact: In London, the police are called the Metropolitan Police, and many people call them «the Met».
fact: In church life, a metropolitan is a senior bishop in charge of an area, especially in Orthodox churches.
exercise: «In 1829 Robert Peel set up London's Metropolitan Police.» What does metropolitan mean in «Metropolitan Police»? | *Belonging to a very big city and the towns around it | Police who work at sea | A police officer who is very tall | Police from a faraway country
exercise: Which of these is a metropolitan area? | A small village in the countryside | *A big city and the towns around it | A desert with no towns at all | A quiet island with one farm
exercise: «Metropolitan Andrey Sheptytsky's network hid Jewish children.» Find and copy the word that shows he was a senior church leader. | hid | *Metropolitan | children | network
test: «Metropolitan France means the main part of France in Europe, not its overseas lands.» What does metropolitan France mean? | *The main part of France in Europe | A tiny French village | All the French lands across the sea | A French car race
test: In church life, what is a metropolitan? | A type of church bell | *A senior bishop in charge of an area | A young priest who is still learning | A city council worker
exam: You meet the new word «metropolitan» in «the Metropolitan Museum of Art». What is the best way to work out its meaning? | *Swap in a meaning, like big city, and see if the sentence still makes sense | Read the sentence backwards | Skip the sentence and never come back to it | Guess that it is a kind of animal
